  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "If we follow the graph from left to right, we can see that: \n\n- For $x\\in (-\\infty ,0)$ the graph rises\n\n- For $x\\in (0,1)$ the graph falls\n\n- For $x\\in (1,\\infty )$ the graph rises\n\nThe function is increasing on the intervals where it never falls: $(-\\infty ,0)$ and $(1,\\infty ).$",
